  "details": "https://youtu.be/5wdaYeozdXU\n\nHave had this repro in a few situations but the most reliable way I've found is to lay down on my side, turn my head/body such that the character model turns, and then turn back. The controller position is offset from the hand of my model. The menu still opens in the correct location (where the controller is actually being tracked), and you can see that the SteamVR menu is showing the controllers in the correct location. When tracked devices are offset in this fashion, any movement snaps the model back to the correct location. \n\nSuspecting this is tied to IK changes.\n\nEdit: Seems moving doesn't always snap back to the correct location if my head is still rotated to the side -- often have to become upright for that to happen. Some kind of weird gimbal thing. ",
